secr <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/secr/index.html>
5.2.0 fixes minor bugs in derived(), sim.capthist()  and
addCovariates(), and a more significant bug in region.N() (R.N ignored
model for density). secr.fit() now allows (relative) density to be
modelled when maximising the conditional likelihood (CL = TRUE) - see the section on relative density in secr-densitysurfaces.pdf <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-densitysurfaces.pdf>.
All changes are listed here <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/secr%205.2.0%20NEWS.txt>.

